          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Warning.</strong> The winner depends on the definition. Upper middle income leads low income by only 0.11 years on the headline. Population weights pick lower middle income, because India, Pakistan, and Bangladesh had women living shorter lives than men in 1960. Ending before COVID picks low income.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Lower middle income is +1.54 with all countries and +1.39 with both-years countries, because West Bank and Gaza has data only from 1990.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Income groups are one recent World Bank label applied to every year, so these are today's groups, not the 1960 groups.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
