      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Warning.</strong> Variability fell in all four groups, so the largest change is a fall. Standard deviation, IQR, and range are in years. Coefficient of variation has no unit. It picks low income because it divides by the group's mean, and that mean rose from a low base.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">China's 33.4 in 1960 could inflate the starting spread. Without China, upper middle income is -3.31, and starting from 1961, 1963, or 1965 gives -3.49, -2.99, and -3.12. It wins every time.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
