          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Warning.</strong> A strong correlation here does not show that one causes the other. Fertility fell and life expectancy rose over the same decades in most countries, and any two trending series correlate: 208 of 217 values are negative, with a median of -0.887.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The <code>yearly_change_pearson</code> column correlates each year's change instead, which removes most of the shared trend. India falls from -0.9973 to -0.027. The median across countries is -0.001, and no country exceeds 0.9 in absolute value.</span></span>"
          }
        }
